# Docker
.dockerignore

# Runtime data (chat history, retrieval store, photos, generated
# state/continuity — all regenerated by the app).
#
# Ignored by directory, never by file name: a name-by-name list only covers
# the kinds of runtime file that existed when it was written, so the next one
# quietly becomes committable. Everything a setting generates lives in its own
# runtime/ directory, which makes the rule one line and the invariant
# checkable — nothing under soul/ is ignored except these:
#
#   git ls-files -ci --exclude-standard soul/   # must print nothing
soul/settings/*/runtime/
debug/

# Legacy: runtime used to live in a parallel data/ tree, outside the setting
# it belonged to. Kept ignored so an un-migrated checkout can't commit it.
/data/

# Frozen correspondence from before the project took its current shape —
# kept on disk, deliberately not versioned: it is raw personal history,
# never read by the engine, and nothing about it benefits from a diff.
/archive/

# macOS
.DS_Store
